'''woodpile''' (wu̇d′pīl), ''n.'' A stack or pile of wood, especially of wood for fuel.
{{smaller block|And, take it in the autumn, what can be pleasanter than to spend a whole day on the sunny side of a barn or a ''woodpile'', chatting with somebody as old as one’s self?
{{right|''Hawthorne'', Seven Gables, iv.}}}}

