'''wood-rush''' (wu̇d′rush), ''n.'' [< ''wood''<sup>1</sup> + ''rush''<sup>1</sup>, ''n.''] A plant of the genus ''Luzula'': also called ''glowworm-grass''. {{smaller|The field wood-rush, ''Luzula campestris'', is an extremely common low plant of Europe and North America, having clusters of brown chaffy flowers appearing early in spring: in Great Britain it is locally called ''blackhead-'' or ''cuckoo-grass'' and ''chimney-sweeps''. A larger species, ''L. sylvatica'', has the names ''wood-blades'' and ''wood-grass''.}}

'''wood-sage''' (wu̇d′sāj), ''n.'' See ''sage''<sup>2</sup>.

